        "original_id": "8c4d2bf8-fa83-5ca5-b7a5-4690aa77e541",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ziggy Marley, Flea, John Frusciante, Michael Peter Balzary, Ken Chastain\n- Products: Dragonfly, Love Is My Religion\n- Organizations: Red Hot Chili Peppers, Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers\n- Roles: musician, actor, bassist, percussionist\n\nFacts:\n- After the 2000 end of Ziggy Marley & The Melody Makers, Ziggy Marley released Dragonfly as his first solo album and Love Is My Religion as his second solo album.\n- On Ziggy Marley's album Dragonfly, the track \"Rainbow in the Sky\" features Flea and John Frusciante of the Red Hot Chili Peppers.\n- On Ziggy Marley's album Dragonfly, the track \"Melancholy Mood\" features only Flea.\n- Michael Peter Balzary, born on 16 October 1962 and better known as Flea, is an Australian-American musician and actor.\n- Flea is best known as the bassist and a founding member of the rock band Red Hot Chili Peppers.\n- Ken Chastain is featured on percussion on Ziggy Marley's album Love Is My Religion.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
